3.3 The While-Loop
The while-loop performs a program (“statement”) as long as certain data conditions (“test expression”) are met. The basic syntax is

while (testexpression)
{
  #increment (i+1);
  statement
}

Here, testexpression is evaluated and the body of the loop is entered if the result is TRUE.

i &lt;- 1

while (i &lt; 6) {
  print(i)
  i = i+1
}

